  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Match the thermodynamics processes taking place in a system with the correct conditions. In the table : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>is the heat supplied, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>W</mi></math> is the work done and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi></math> is change in internal energy of the system.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 350px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>Process</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>Condition</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(I)</td>\t\t\t<td>Adiabatic</td>\t\t\t<td>(A)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(II)</td>\t\t\t<td>Isothermal</td>\t\t\t<td>(B)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(III)</td>\t\t\t<td>Isochoric</td>\t\t\t<td>(C)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(IV)</td>\t\t\t<td>\t\t\t<p>Isobaric</p>\t\t\t</td>\t\t\t<td>(D)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "(I) - (A), (II) - (B), (III) - (D), (IV) - (D)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "(I) - (B), (II) - (A), (III) - (D), (IV) - (C)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "(I) - (A), (II) - (A), (III) - (B), (IV) - (C)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "(I) - (B), (II) - (D), (III) - (A), (IV) - (C)",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In Adiabatic&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;Exchange of heat does not take place.</p><p>In Isothermal&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;Temperature does not change therefore internal energy also remains constant.</p><p>In Isochoric&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;Volume remains constant therefore work done is zero.</p><p>In Isobaric&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>V</mi></math>, Volume changes so work done is not equal to zero.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>V</mi></math>, Volume changes therefore internal energy changes.<br />&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>T</mi></math>, Temperature changes therefore heat also changes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
}